==Enemy==
This [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] [[warp]]s back any cat it touches except for [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]], and has an above-average range which nullifies the effectiveness of many [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien units]]. Its attack power is relatively low compared to other Cyclones, but its 100% chance to Warp cats and rather high range for a Cyclone allows it to easily gain ground.

Unlike the [[Cosmic Cyclone]], Super Cosmic Cyclone is not a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy.

==Strategy==
Before attempting to fight this enemy in [[The 2nd Dimension]], it is recommended to have all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from at least one [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapter to reduce the Super Cosmic Cyclone's stats and make it more manageable. In [[Revenge of the Wormhole (Merciless)|Revenge of the Wormhole]], it is buffed to 600% and has support from 900% [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s, nearly necessitating all Anti-Starred Alien Treasures from all three CotC chapters, which in turn will also make the previous stages far easier.

[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] will have no chance of hitting this Cyclone unless it is frozen/cursed from other sources due to his inferior range and lack of Warp Immunity (unless his Immune to Warp [[Talents|Talent]] has been unlocked). If the player has [[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Voli]], it can be used in Castaway Cat's place, as Voli has Immune to Warp and is able to consistently delay Super Cosmic Cyclone. [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]] is very effective with his high range and ability to Slow Aliens.

Neo Psychocat and [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs Cat]] are quite effective at impeding its advance, while ranged attackers like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] can be stacked to deal damage.

[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] is an effective meatshield due to its Warp Immunity and Strong vs. Aliens, but if the Cyclone is sufficiently buffed, it can quickly mow them down regardless.

